      "content": "In your low-fat mayo prototype, alternative emulsifiers or stabilizers could potentially handle the acidity better than lecithin. Xanthan gum, as you mentioned, is a good option, as it can interact with negatively charged surfaces, such as lecithin, to stabilize emulsions. Calcium stearate, a negatively charged phospholipid, could also be effective, but might be more expensive and have similar pH constraints as lecithin. Additionally, gum arabic, starch-based options, and other polysaccharides may also exhibit similar stabilization behaviors in acidic environments.",
